%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e3183497ef65af040907ea31c64f3fe1, type: 3}
  m_Name: Story
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: OldGods.Runtime::OldGods.Runtime.StoryText
  Premise: 'Before anyone held the throne, there were the old gods. Many of them, each with a domain and a people.


    Between them stood a throne no one had claimed. It stood empty through every age, guarded by a construct they called The Last Test.


    Now the old gods walk the road to it. Some go to see it. Some go to break its guardian. One will sit.'
  GodLines:
  - Id: god.storm
    Text: The sky gathers behind you.
  - Id: god.forge
    Text: The fire in your hands has never gone out.
  - Id: god.tide
    Text: The water remembers where it is going.
  - Id: god.hunt
    Text: You have already chosen your mark.
  - Id: god.ember
    Text: A small flame, walking a long road.
  - Id: god.earth
    Text: Each step is a promise to the ground.
  - Id: god.elias
    Text: You believe the throne should be taken. You walk to take it.
  BiomeLines:
  - Id: biome.grey_steppe
    Text: The first road, and the wall that guards it.
  - Id: biome.ash_wood
    Text: It burned, and it has not stopped burning.
  - Id: biome.drowned_coast
    Text: The sea takes, and keeps.
  - Id: biome.last_test
    Text: The throne waits.
  - Id: biome.greybox
    Text: A place to learn the road.
  EliasEnding:
  - Elias climbs to the throne. No one has sat here before him.
  - He sits because he believes it is right.
  - The power of the old gods flows into him. One by one, they are gone from the world.
  - They live on in him. The throne is empty no longer.
  RefusedEnding:
  - The Last Test falls.
  - The throne does not answer you. It was never meant for you.
  - Somewhere behind you, Elias is still walking.
  Fragments:
  - Id: lore.empty_seat
    BiomeId: biome.grey_steppe
    Title: The Empty Seat
    Text: No god ever sat the throne. The old gods walked past it for ages, each of them sure it was meant for someone else.
  - Id: lore.wardens_wall
    BiomeId: biome.grey_steppe
    Title: The Warden's Wall
    Text: The Stone Warden was raised to keep the steppe's first road. When the road was forgotten, it kept walking the wall anyway.
  - Id: lore.many_gods
    BiomeId: biome.grey_steppe
    Title: Many Gods
    Text: There were many of us once. Storm and Forge, Tide and Hunt, Ember and Earth, and others whose names the grass has taken. None of us ruled. That was the point.
  - Id: lore.the_burning
    BiomeId: biome.ash_wood
    Title: The Burning
    Text: The wood burned in a quarrel between gods that no one now remembers starting. The stag walked out of the fire, and it has not stopped burning since.
  - Id: lore.quiet_god
    BiomeId: biome.ash_wood
    Title: A Quiet God
    Text: Elias was the quietest of us. He listened more than he spoke. Some of us mistook that for weakness.
  - Id: lore.ash_and_memory
    BiomeId: biome.ash_wood
    Title: Ash and Memory
    Text: Fire keeps what it takes. Stand close to the old embers and you can hear the gods arguing about the throne.
  - Id: lore.what_the_sea_kept
    BiomeId: biome.drowned_coast
    Title: What the Sea Kept
    Text: 'The Tide Mother keeps everything the sea takes: ships, songs, the dead. She does not give them back. She thinks of it as care.'
  - Id: lore.the_construct
    BiomeId: biome.drowned_coast
    Title: The Last Test
    Text: Someone made a guardian for the throne and called it The Last Test. It keeps the throne from the unworthy. No one remembers who made it, or who made the throne.
  - Id: lore.the_choice
    BiomeId: biome.drowned_coast
    Title: The Choice
    Text: We could share the world, or let one of us hold it. We argued for an age. In the end one of us decided, and the rest of us followed him there.
